  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U9L-READ-1",
      "title": "The Typhoon Night",
      "text": "Last September a strong typhoon hit our town. The weather forecast said it would come after midnight, and every TV station broadcast the news all day. At the supermarket, people squeezed into the aisles to buy food and batteries. That night the wind was crazy. The power went out at ten, so our air-conditioner stopped and the room got hot. A small fire broke out in a shop down the street, but the firemen put it out in ten minutes. My little brother cut his finger on a broken cup. He saw the blood and almost passed out. In the morning, the news said the water almost broke through the old dam near the border of our city. Cleaning the streets was difficult, but our neighbors shared their tools and finished the work by noon."
    }
  ],
